{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler/stitch code generation pipeline task (#5518). The task is to implement `cmd/base64/main.go` — specifically the **encoding mode only** (srd080-base64 requirements R1.1 through R1.4). The task does NOT include decoding mode (R2.x). The implementation must use `pkg/encutil.Encode` with `EncoderConfig` for the encoding logic, `pkg/encutil.OpenInput` for file/stdin handling, and `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at startup. The file must be created from scratch following project conventions.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go Unix utilities reimplementation project with differential testing against GNU reference binaries\n   - `pkg/encutil` package provides shared encoding/decoding infrastructure: `EncoderConfig`, `Encode()`, `OpenInput()`\n   - `pkg/sys` provides `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling matching GNU coreutils behavior\n   - RFC 4648 Base64 encoding via Go's `encoding/base64` stdlib package\n   - Default wrap column of 76 characters; `-w 0` disables wrapping\n   - Flag parsing for `-w`/`--wrap` column width\n   - File or stdin input (`-` means stdin, no args means stdin)\n   - Exit code 1 on file open errors with stderr message\n   - 40-line function limit (E8), 500-line file limit (E9)\n   - SPDX copyright header required on every Go file\n   - No git commands allowed; orchestrator handles git externally\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd080-base64.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for base64 utility covering encoding (R1) and decoding (R2)\n     - Task only covers R1.1-R1.4 (encoding mode)\n     - R1.1: Read from FILE or stdin, encode RFC 4648 Base64, write to stdout\n     - R1.2: Wrap at 76 chars by default\n     - R1.3: `-w COLS` / `--wrap=COLS` sets wrap column; `-w 0` disables wrapping\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 when named file cannot be opened, error to stderr\n     - Non-goals: no Base64url, no Base32\n   \n   - `pkg/encutil/encode.go` (provided inline in context)\n     - Key exports: `EncoderConfig{Encode func([]byte) string, WrapCol int}`, `Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error`\n     - `Encode` reads all input, applies cfg.Encode, wraps at cfg.WrapCol (0 means no wrap)\n     - `writeWrapped` handles line-wrapping logic internally\n\n   - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` (provided inline in context)\n     - Key export: `OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` — returns os.Stdin for \"\" or \"-\", otherwise os.Open\n     - `DecoderConfig` and `Decode` also available but not needed for this task\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (provided inline in context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` — installs SIGPIPE handler that exits 0\n\n   - `cmd/base64/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - The sole deliverable file for this task\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. No code was written. Only the SRD was read before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the full SRD to understand requirements beyond what was provided in the task description. Confirmed the encoding requirements R1.1-R1.4 match the task scope. Noted that the SRD also has decoding (R2) and exit code/SIGPIPE (R3) requirements, but this task only covers R1.1-R1.4 encoding plus the SIGPIPE handler (per design decision D3).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Massive task description including role definition, repository file listing, project context (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, roadmap, analysis, source code), requirement states, task details (#5518 — implement cmd/base64 encoding mode), execution constitution, go style constitution, shared protocols, package contracts, constraints, and description with requirements R1-R4, design decisions D1-D3, and acceptance criteria AC1-AC5.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Request to create a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/base64/main.go` implementing Base64 encoding mode (R1.1-R1.4)\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/base64 ./cmd/base64/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/base64/`\n   - Test that `echo 'hello' | go run ./cmd/base64/` produces valid Base64 output\n   - Verify default wrap column is 76 and `-w 0` disables wrapping\n   - Verify file arguments and stdin both work\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd080-base64.yaml`) and was about to write `cmd/base64/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The implementation plan is:\n   - Use `encoding/base64.StdEncoding.EncodeToString` as the Encode function for `encutil.EncoderConfig`\n   - Parse `-w`/`--wrap` flag with default value 76\n   - Use `flag` package for CLI parsing (not cobra, since other cmd/ utilities in the project use simple flag parsing)\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first in main\n   - Use `encutil.OpenInput()` for each file arg (or stdin if no args/\"-\")\n   - Use `encutil.Encode()` with the configured `EncoderConfig`\n   - Exit 1 with stderr error message on file open failures\n   - Add SPDX copyright header\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/base64/main.go` implementing the Base64 encoding mode. The task description states: \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.1 -- parse command-line flags for -w/--wrap column width\", \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.2 -- encode stdin or file arguments to Base64 and write to stdout\", \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.3 -- wrap encoded output at column 76 by default, configurable via -w; -w 0 disables wrapping\", \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.4 -- read from stdin when no file arguments are given or when the file argument is '-'\". Design decisions specify: \"Use pkg/encutil.Encode with an EncoderConfig whose Encode field is set to standard Base64 encoding and WrapCol is set from the -w flag (default 76)\", \"Use pkg/encutil.OpenInput for file/stdin handling\", \"Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\". After writing the file, verify with `go build -o bin/base64 ./cmd/base64/` and `go vet ./cmd/base64/`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5518/9823db9b-987d-4a1a-9f55-dd37cda1278f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9823db9b-987d-4a1a-9f55-dd37cda1278f","uuid":"87f926a0-d86f-40e7-8ddb-68903d8875dd","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:46:24.179Z","isSynthetic":true}
