{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TtEZDvWuz2g46ZzePsWPxQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage encutil\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"io\"\n8\t\t\"os\"\n9\t\t\"strings\"\n10\t)\n11\t\n12\t// DecoderConfig parameterizes a decoding operation with the decoding function\n13\t// and garbage-handling behavior.\n14\t// R2.1: Decode converts an encoded string back to raw bytes.\n15\t// R2.1: IgnoreGarbage skips non-alphabet characters in the input.\n16\ttype DecoderConfig struct {\n17\t\tDecode        func(string) ([]byte, error)\n18\t\tIgnoreGarbage bool\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\t// Decode reads encoded input from r, decodes it using cfg, and writes the raw\n22\t// bytes to w.\n23\t// R2.2: reads all input, strips whitespace, decodes via cfg.Decode, writes to w.\n24\t// R2.3: returns error on invalid characters when IgnoreGarbage is false.\n25\tfunc Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error {\n26\t\tdata, err := io.ReadAll(r)\n27\t\tif err != nil {\n28\t\t\treturn err\n29\t\t}\n30\t\tinput := stripWhitespace(string(data))\n31\t\tif cfg.IgnoreGarbage {\n32\t\t\tinput = stripGarbage(input)\n33\t\t}\n34\t\tdecoded, err := cfg.Decode(input)\n35\t\tif err != nil {\n36\t\t\treturn err\n37\t\t}\n38\t\t_, err = w.Write(decoded)\n39\t\treturn err\n40\t}\n41\t\n42\tfunc stripWhitespace(s string) string {\n43\t\tvar b strings.Builder\n44\t\tb.Grow(len(s))\n45\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(s); i++ {\n46\t\t\tch := s[i]\n47\t\t\tif ch != ' ' && ch != '\\t' && ch != '\\n' && ch != '\\r' {\n48\t\t\t\tb.WriteByte(ch)\n49\t\t\t}\n50\t\t}\n51\t\treturn b.String()\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\t// stripGarbage removes characters not in the common base-encoding superset\n55\t// alphabet (A-Za-z0-9+/=-_), covering Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex,\n56\t// and Base16.\n57\tfunc stripGarbage(s string) string {\n58\t\tvar b strings.Builder\n59\t\tb.Grow(len(s))\n60\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(s); i++ {\n61\t\t\tif isEncodingAlphabet(s[i]) {\n62\t\t\t\tb.WriteByte(s[i])\n63\t\t\t}\n64\t\t}\n65\t\treturn b.String()\n66\t}\n67\t\n68\tfunc isEncodingAlphabet(ch byte) bool {\n69\t\treturn (ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z') ||\n70\t\t\t(ch >= 'a' && ch <= 'z') ||\n71\t\t\t(ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') ||\n72\t\t\tch == '+' || ch == '/' || ch == '=' ||\n73\t\t\tch == '-' || ch == '_'\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\t// OpenInput opens a file for reading, or returns os.Stdin when filename is\n77\t// empty or \"-\".\n78\t// R3.1: returns an io.ReadCloser for the named file or stdin.\n79\t// R3.2: returns an error when the file cannot be opened.\n80\tfunc OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error) {\n81\t\tif filename == \"\" || filename == \"-\" {\n82\t\t\treturn os.Stdin, nil\n83\t\t}\n84\t\treturn os.Open(filename)\n85\t}\n86\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VAtkHfv76TMxPb4eXCkL9C","session_id":"9823db9b-987d-4a1a-9f55-dd37cda1278f","uuid":"293846bc-7263-4060-b75b-84992e4ef34f","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:46:38.201Z"}
