{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VAtkHfv76TMxPb4eXCkL9C","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with a comprehensive report.\n\n## Flag Parsing Pattern Analysis\n\n**The repo uses MANUAL flag parsing** - no pflag or standard flag library. All utilities implement custom parsing logic.\n\n### Flag Parsing Patterns Found\n\n#### 1. **split/main.go** (Most Complex Example)\nThe most comprehensive flag parsing example with both long and short flags:\n\n**Approach:**\n- Manual iteration through `os.Args[1:]`\n- Separates long flags (`--`) from short flags (`-`)\n- Has dedicated functions for each type:\n  - `parseLongFlag()` handles `--flag` and `--flag=value` syntax\n  - `parseShortFlags()` handles combined short flags like `-abc`\n  - `longOptValue()` extracts values from either `--flag=val` or next argument\n  - `extractFlagValue()` handles short flag values\n\n**Flag Style:**\n- Long flags: `--lines`, `--bytes`, `--line-bytes`, `--number`, `--suffix-length`, `--numeric-suffixes`, `--additional-suffix`, `--filter`\n- Short flags: `-l`, `-b`, `-C`, `-n`, `-a`, `-d`\n- Both boolean flags (`-d`) and flags requiring values\n- Handles `--` for end-of-flags marker\n- Supports combined short flags: `-abc` treated as separate `-a -b -c`\n\n#### 2. **expand/main.go** (Simple Example)\nSimpler manual parsing:\n\n**Approach:**\n- Basic loop through args\n- Checks for `-t` or `-t<value>` patterns\n- Manual string prefix checking\n- No long flag support\n\n**Flag Style:**\n- Only short flags: `-t`\n- Optional combined syntax: `-t8` or `-t 8`\n\n#### 3. **cat/main.go** (Simplest Example)\nMinimal boolean-only flags:\n\n**Approach:**\n- Simple character loop: `for _, c := range arg[1:]`\n- All flags are boolean\n- Single-pass processing with switch statements\n- No value-bearing flags\n\n**Flag Style:**\n- Only short boolean flags: `-n`, `-b`, `-s`, `-v`, `-E`, `-T`, `-A`\n- Supports combined flags: `-nv` treated as `-n -v`\n- No long flag support needed\n\n---\n\n## Function Signatures from pkg/encutil\n\n### encode.go\n```go\ntype EncoderConfig struct {\n\tEncode  func([]byte) string\n\tWrapCol int\n}\n\nfunc Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error\n```\n\n**Details:**\n- Takes an `io.Reader` (input), `io.Writer` (output), and config\n- `cfg.Encode`: function reference that converts `[]byte` to `string`\n- `cfg.WrapCol`: line wrapping column (0 = no wrapping, single-line output)\n- Returns error on I/O failures\n- Always adds trailing newline after output\n\n### decode.go\n```go\ntype DecoderConfig struct {\n\tDecode        func(string) ([]byte, error)\n\tIgnoreGarbage bool\n}\n\nfunc Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error\n\nfunc OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)\n```\n\n**Details:**\n- `Decode()`: Takes `io.Reader` (input), `io.Writer` (output), and config\n- `cfg.Decode`: function reference that converts `string` to `([]byte, error)`\n- `cfg.IgnoreGarbage`: boolean to skip non-alphabet characters\n- `OpenInput()`: Opens file or returns stdin; returns `io.ReadCloser` and error\n  - Treats empty string `\"\"` same as `\"-\"` (both return stdin)\n  - Used for handling `--input-file` style flags\n\n---\n\n## Summary for Your Implementation\n\nFor a new utility with `--wrap/-w` style flags, follow this pattern:\n\n1. **Manual parsing function** with structure like split's approach:\n   - Iterate through args with index tracking\n   - Separate handling for long vs short flags\n   - Helper functions for value extraction\n   \n2. **Use `OpenInput(filename)`** from encutil for file handling (already available)\n\n3. **Use `Encode()` or `Decode()`** from encutil, passing an `EncoderConfig` or `DecoderConfig` with appropriate function reference and options\n\n4. **For `--wrap/-w`**: Add to `parseShortFlags()` as a value-bearing flag (`-w <cols>`) and to `parseLongFlag()` with both `--wrap=<cols>` and `--wrap <cols>` syntax\n\nAbsolute file paths:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5518/cmd/split/main.go` (most complete example)\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5518/pkg/encutil/encode.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5518/pkg/encutil/decode.go`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9823db9b-987d-4a1a-9f55-dd37cda1278f","uuid":"9831fddb-9d1d-4c8d-b752-e1e5435dd9e8","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:46:51.618Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5518, I need to understand how existing cmd/ utilities parse flags (especially --wrap/-w style long/short flags). Look at 2-3 existing cmd/*/main.go files that use flag parsing — particularly any that handle encoding or have similar flag styles. Also read pkg/encutil/encode.go and pkg/encutil/decode.go fully to see OpenInput and Encode signatures. Report the flag parsing pattern used (pflag? standard flag? manual parsing?) and the exact function signatures from encutil.","agentId":"af58167342ce2ebe7","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with a comprehensive report.\n\n## Flag Parsing Pattern Analysis\n\n**The repo uses MANUAL flag parsing** - no pflag or standard flag library. All utilities implement custom parsing logic.\n\n### Flag Parsing Patterns Found\n\n#### 1. **split/main.go** (Most Complex Example)\nThe most comprehensive flag parsing example with both long and short flags:\n\n**Approach:**\n- Manual iteration through `os.Args[1:]`\n- Separates long flags (`--`) from short flags (`-`)\n- Has dedicated functions for each type:\n  - `parseLongFlag()` handles `--flag` and `--flag=value` syntax\n  - `parseShortFlags()` handles combined short flags like